### STEP 03
Date: 2026-09-08
Phase: 2
Step: 03 (Bug Fix)

Files Modified:
- src/scenes/CharacterSelectScene.js
- src/scenes/VehicleSelectScene.js
- src/scenes/StageSelectScene.js

Bug Found:
- Character Select → Vehicle Select navigation not working
- Vehicle Select → Stage Select navigation not working
- Stage Select → GameScene navigation not working

Root Cause:
- In all three selection scenes, the `createXxxGrid()` method was called recursively when a card was clicked
- The recursive call reset `this.selectedCharacter/Vehicle/Stage = null` at the start of the method
- This caused the selection to be lost before the SELECT button could use it

Exact Fix:
1. Removed the recursive call to `createXxxGrid()` from the card click handler
2. Added a new `updateCardSelection()` method that only updates the visual selection state
3. Changed card click handler to call `updateCardSelection()` instead of `createXxxGrid()`
4. Added proper cleanup of existing cards before recreating the grid

Testing Performed:
- Verified all three scene files have valid JavaScript syntax
- Started Vite dev server on port 3005 without errors
- Navigation flow should now work: Character → Vehicle → Stage → Game

Result:
- Navigation between selection scenes should now work correctly
- Selected character/vehicle/stage is preserved when clicking cards
- SELECT/NEXT buttons should transition to the next scene

Remaining issues:
- Need to manually test in browser to confirm navigation works
- May need to fine-tune physics values for better gameplay feel

