### STEP 04
Date: 2026-09-08
Phase: 2
Step: 04 (Bug Fix - Navigation Still Not Working)

Files Modified:
- src/scenes/CharacterSelectScene.js (complete rewrite)
- src/scenes/VehicleSelectScene.js (complete rewrite)
- src/scenes/StageSelectScene.js (complete rewrite)

Bug Found:
- Character Select → Vehicle Select navigation still not working after previous fix
- The issue was that old card elements (especially hit zones) were not being destroyed when the grid was recreated
- Old hit zones were overlapping with new ones, blocking click events

Root Cause:
- When a card was clicked, `createCharacterGrid(x, y)` was called to refresh the display
- This created new card elements on top of the old ones
- The old hit zones were still active and blocking the new ones from receiving click events
- This caused the click to not register on the new cards

Exact Fix:
1. Added `this.cardElements` array to store all created elements
2. Before recreating the grid, all old elements are destroyed using `el.destroy()`
3. This ensures no overlapping elements remain
4. The grid is then recreated with fresh elements

Testing Performed:
- Verified all three scene files have valid JavaScript syntax
- Started Vite dev server on port 3001 without errors
- Navigation flow should now work: Character → Vehicle → Stage → Game

Result:
- Navigation between selection scenes should now work correctly
- Selected character/vehicle/stage is preserved when clicking cards
- No overlapping elements to block click events

Remaining issues:
- Need to manually test in browser to confirm navigation works
- May need to fine-tune physics values for better gameplay feel

